# Unsplash Image Integration Guide

## Basic Usage

When generating image elements, use Unsplash's source API with the following format:

```
https://source.unsplash.com/{WIDTH}x{HEIGHT}/?{KEYWORDS}
```

## React Component Format

For React components, use this format:

```tsx
// Basic usage
<img
  src="https://source.unsplash.com/800x600/?nature"
  alt="Description"
  className="w-full h-auto rounded-lg"
/>

// With loading optimization
<img
  src="https://source.unsplash.com/800x600/?nature"
  alt="Description"
  loading="lazy"
  className="w-full h-auto rounded-lg object-cover"
/>
```

## Default Settings

- Default size: 800x600
- Default keyword: 'random'
- Default Tailwind classes: 'w-full h-auto rounded-lg'

## Common Sizes

- Thumbnail: 200x200
- Card: 400x300
- Hero: 1200x600
- Profile: 150x150

## Examples

### Hero Image
```tsx
<img
  src="https://source.unsplash.com/1200x600/?landscape"
  alt="Hero landscape"
  className="w-full h-[600px] object-cover"
/>
```

### Card Image
```tsx
<img
  src="https://source.unsplash.com/400x300/?business"
  alt="Business card image"
  className="w-full aspect-video object-cover rounded-t-lg"
/>
```

### Avatar/Profile
```tsx
<img
  src="https://source.unsplash.com/150x150/?portrait"
  alt="Profile picture"
  className="w-12 h-12 rounded-full object-cover"
/>
```

## Best Practices

1. Always include descriptive alt text
2. Use `loading="lazy"` for images below the fold
3. Specify exact dimensions to prevent layout shift
4. Use appropriate Tailwind classes for responsive behavior
5. Consider using blur placeholder with next/image if using Next.js

## Keywords

Common keyword combinations:
- Nature: nature,landscape,forest
- Business: business,office,corporate
- Technology: technology,computer,digital
- People: people,portrait,face
- Food: food,restaurant,cooking

Note: Multiple keywords should be comma-separated without spaces.
